<title>UK: Guardian leads sector down after downgrade.</title>
<headline>Guardian leads sector down after downgrade.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Guardian Royal led the insurance sector lower on Monday after Dresdner Kleinwort Benson downgraded the stock before the group reports its annual results tomorrow, dealers said.</p>
<p>By 1014 GMT, the shares were down 6p to 283-1/2p.</p>
<p>Shares in General Accident tumbled 19-1/2p to 799-1/2, while shares in Commercial Union fell 17-1/2p to 691.</p>
